# JiraWM — Cline Rules

## Role
Cline executes file-level changes, builds, and TypeScript checks.
Architecture decisions happen in Claude.ai project chat — not here.

## Before every task
1. Read CLAUDE.md fully
2. Check current file state before editing — never reconstruct from memory
3. Run npx tsc --noEmit after changes — report errors before declaring done

## Task scope
- One concern per task
- Stop and report if a change would affect more than 3 files unexpectedly
- Never install new npm packages without explicit instruction

## Build loop
npm run build → check for errors → report result
Never run dev server.

## Agents
- Default: standard Cline for most tasks
- Complex Jira API parsing / Service Worker lifecycle issues: flag for Kimi handoff
- Architecture questions: flag for Claude.ai chat

## Commit message format
feat: [phase] brief description
fix: brief description
chore: brief description

## TypeScript
Strict mode is on. Fix all errors — never use @ts-ignore or any casts without explicit approval.

## chrome.storage pattern
import { storage } from '../lib/storage';
Always go through the storage wrapper, never call chrome.storage directly in components.
